{1}{What brings you to our tribe, boy? Where did you get the head band?}{What brings you to our tribe, sister? Are you here to join with us?}{}{}{}{}
{2}{It was given to me by a poor woman who wishes to join you.}{1}{5}{lf1 0}{10}{lf1 1}
{3}{I'm here to help a poor woman who wishes to join with you.}{0}{5}{lf1 0}{75}{lf1 1}
{4}{Hurgha?}{}{-4}{}{0}{fl 124}
{10}{Why is she not here herself?}{Why is she not here herself?}{}{}{}{}
{11}{She is not able to escape from the southern encampment.}{}{5}{}{20}{}
{20}{We do not need those that cannot fend for themselves.}{You were able to escape. We do not need those that cannot fend for themselves.}{}{}{}{}
{21}{So you would simply leave her to rot?}{}{5}{}{30}{}
{22}{What message would you have me bring to her, then?}{}{5}{}{85}{}
{23}{I'll be on my way, then.}{}{5}{}{105}{}
{30}{Perhaps you don't realize where you are. Look around. This is a wasteland that devours the unprepared, at least she is protected in the encampment. We can not afford to have someone who needs to be helped along.}{Perhaps you don't realize where you are. Look around. This is a wasteland that devours the unprepared, at least she is protected in the encampment. We can not afford to have someone who needs to be helped along.}{}{}{}{}
{31}{What should I tell her? That you don't care she's suffering?}{}{5}{}{40}{}
{32}{I can see your point. I'll be off, then.}{}{5}{}{105}{}
{40}{I feel for her, but out here feelings mean nothing. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{I feel for her, but out here feelings mean nothing. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{}{}{}{in-2013}
{41}{Charging the gates with that pistol would be suicide.}{}{5}{}{50}{}
{42}{You can either help her or die where you stand, wench!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{49}{Thank you for that, at least. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{gf2136 1}
{50}{Better to die fighting than to live a torturous life.}{Better to die fighting than to live a torturous life.}{}{}{}{}
{51}{I do not think she will be relieved to hear that.}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{52}{I'd like to test that by killing you right now, you heartless swine!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{60}{Such is life. Is there anything else?}{Such is life. Is there anything else?}{}{}{}{gf2136 1}
{61}{May I ask about you? What is your story?}{}{5}{ch-13}{115}{}
{62}{May I ask about you? What is your story?}{}{5}{ch14}{125}{}
{69}{I suppose not. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{70}{You have just assured your death, fool!}{You have just assured your death, fool!}{}{}{}{}
{75}{Why has she sent you? Why is she not here herself?}{Why has she sent you? Why is she not here herself?}{}{}{}{}
{76}{She is not able to escape from the southern encampment.}{}{5}{}{20}{}
{85}{Tell her it is better to die fighting than to live in captivity.}{Tell her it is better to die fighting than to live in captivity.}{}{}{}{}
{86}{I don't believe that is the answer she was looking for.}{}{5}{}{95}{}
{87}{I'd like to test that by killing you right now, you heartless swine!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{95}{I feel for her, but out here feelings mean nothing. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{I feel for her, but out here feelings mean nothing. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{}{}{}{in-2013}
{96}{Charging the gates with that pistol would be suicide.}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{97}{You can either help her or die where you stand, wench!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{98}{Thank you for that, at least. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{gf2136 1}
{105}{Do not think me completely heartless. Things are what they are, and there is naught to be done about it. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{Do not think me completely heartless. Things are what they are, and there is naught to be done about it. I can give you this old pistol to bring to her [she hands you an old, rusty pistol]. Tell her to use it to escape, if she means to join up with us.}{}{}{}{}
{106}{Charging the gates with that pistol would be suicide.}{}{5}{}{50}{}
{107}{You can either help her or die where you stand, wench!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{114}{Thank you for that, at least. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{gf2136 1}
{115}{I will not discuss things of that sort with outsiders.}{I will not discuss things of that sort with outsiders.}{}{}{}{}
{116}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{124}{A blithering idiot! Leave this area, fool. You are not welcome here.}{A blithering idiot! Leave this area, fool. You are not welcome here.}{}{}{}{}
{125}{I was sent here for killing a man that was beating me and I refused to be trapped in the men's encampment when I arrived. My women have either escaped the encampment or avoided it altogether from the time they arrived.}{I was sent here for killing a man that was beating me and I refused to be trapped in the men's encampment when I arrived. My women have either escaped the encampment or avoided it altogether from the time they arrived.}{}{}{}{}
{126}{That's quite the tale. I will be on my way, now. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{127}{They should have put you down like the dog you are, wench!}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 70 ,co}
{135}{What do you want now?}{What do you want now?}{}{}{}{}
{136}{This is the woman I told you about. She wishes to join you.}{}{5}{pa6571}{145}{}
{137}{Nothing, I suppose.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{145}{Thank you for helping her, even though I am not sure it was in her best interest. As I said before, she will be dead if she can not fend for herself out here.}{Thank you for helping her, even though I am not sure it was in her best interest. As I said before, she will be dead if she can not fend for herself out here.}{}{}{}{}
{146}{So you will let her join you?}{}{5}{}{155}{}
{147}{You're a rather happy sort, aren't you?}{}{5}{}{165}{}
{155}{She may stay with us, yes.}{She may stay with us, yes.}{}{}{}{lf3 1}
{156}{A:}{}{5}{}{-10}{}
{165}{[She scowls at you.] This is not a laughing matter. You had best start treating your situation with the seriousness it warrants, or you'll be dead.}{[She scowls at you.] This is not a laughing matter. You had best start treating your situation with the seriousness it warrants, or you'll be dead.}{}{}{}{lf3 1}
{166}{Are you threatening me?}{}{5}{}{175}{}
{167}{You're right. I should not make light of this situation.}{}{5}{}{185}{}
{175}{Not at all, nor do I need to. This blighted land will take care of you in its own time, if you do not pay it the proper respect.}{Not at all, nor do I need to. This blighted land will take care of you in its own time, if you do not pay it the proper respect.}{}{}{}{}
{176}{So you will let her join you?}{}{5}{}{155}{}
{185}{Remember that. This blighted land will destroy you if you do not pay it the proper respect.}{Remember that. This blighted land will destroy you if you do not pay it the proper respect.}{}{}{}{}
{186}{So you will let her join you?}{}{5}{}{155}{}
{194}{Thank you for bringing Cynthia here.}{Thank you for bringing Cynthia here.}{}{}{}{}

